  "statement": "Roman numerals are represented by seven symbols: I (1), V (5), X (10), L (50), C (100), D (500), and M (1000). Subtractive notation applies when a smaller numeral precedes a larger numeral (e.g. IV = 4, IX = 9, XL = 40, XC = 90, CD = 400, CM = 900).\n\nGiven a valid Roman numeral string S, convert and print its integer value.",
  "inputFormat": "A single string S.",
  "outputFormat": "Print the converted integer.",
  "constraints": "1 <= |S| <= 15, value in range [1, 3999]",
